==English==
[[File:Pirogues_Madagascar.jpg|thumb|pirogues (1), Madagascar]]

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|fr|pirogue}}, in turn from {{der|en|es|piragua}}, from {{der|en|car|piraua}}. {{doublet|en|periagua}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/pəˈɹəʊɡ/|/pɪˈɹəʊɡ/}}
* {{rhymes|en|əʊɡ|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[canoe]] of [[shallow]] [[draft]], made by hollowing a log.
#: {{syn|en|periagua}}
# A small [[flat-bottom]] [[boat]] of shallow draft. <!--Specifically, a flat-bottom boat made out of a four-foot by eight-foot piece of plywood, the bottom being a two-foot eight-inch-wide eight-foot-long pointed-end lengthwise-centered oval cut from the piece, and the boat's sides being the two remaining pieces attached lengthwise to the outside edges of the oval.-->
# {{lb|en|Cajun cooking}} A boat-shaped food that is stuffed with seafood.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1996 | title=Walt Disney World for Lovers |author=Rick Perlmutter, Gayle Perlmutter | page=240| passage=There are even more elaborately prepared Cajun specialties, such as Bayou Bouillabaisse and '''pirogue''' of pasta and seafood. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1999 | title=Fodor's 2000 USA |author=| page=484| passage=The eggplant '''pirogue''', a regional specialty, is especially good here.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2005|month=August|work=Indianapolis Monthly |title=Restaurants|author=|volume=|page=300|passage=Diners love the '''pirogue''' bread with crawfish tails, the barbecue shrimp with fiery tasso and the banana bread pudding.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2019 | title=Continuum|author=Marlys Beider | page=257| passage=She had ordered eggplant '''pirogue''' — a hollowed out eggplant, breaded, fried, and stuffed with shrimp, crawfish, and crab.}}

